        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75256866?u=e8b7f1039e5b3d31d8f1d9a206b6046d6c684fc8&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<p dir=\"auto\">dialog: Add touch dismissal bug notes for closedby in Chrome and Firefox</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #30474.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5418797612\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30474\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30474/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30474\">#30474</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds bug notes to <code class=\"notranslate\">html.elements.dialog.closedby</code> regarding a touch-dismissal bug where tapping the backdrop dismisses the dialog while propagating click events to interactive elements behind the backdrop:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Chrome</strong>: Tapping backdrop caused click-through before Chrome 154 (<a href=\"https://crbug.com/425579196\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chromium issue 425579196</a>). Fixed in Chrome 154 (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6209615938322432\" rel=\"nofollow\">ChromeStatus 6209615938322432</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>Firefox</strong>: Tapping backdrop dismisses the dialog while triggering a click on elements behind the backdrop (<a href=\"https://bugzil.la/2022750\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bugzilla 2022750</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Per maintainer feedback in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5418797612\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30474\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30474/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30474\">#30474</a>, this behavior is documented in release/support notes rather than marking partial implementation.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Document known browser behavior and bug tracking for developers using <code class=\"notranslate\">closedby</code> with touch interaction.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30737",
            "title": "dialog: Add touch dismissal bug notes for closedby in Chrome and Firefox",
